@namespace Showcase.Web.Client.Pages

@page "/fa-table/api"

<DemoPageHeader Title="Table: API" ComponentName="FaTable" DocSlug="fa-table" />

<ComponentSubNav BaseRoute="/fa-table" />

<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>Columns</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyList&lt;string&gt;</code></td><td>required — header text, defines column order</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>Rows</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyList&lt;IReadOnlyDictionary&lt;string, RenderFragment&gt;&gt;</code></td><td>required — one dictionary per row, keyed by column name; a missing key renders an empty cell</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>CssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>AdditionalAttributes</code></td><td><code>IReadOnlyDictionary&lt;string, object&gt;?</code></td><td>any attribute not listed above splats straight onto the <code>&lt;table&gt;</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>
    You own paging/filtering — FaGrid is the step up that owns that loop itself.
    Each generated <code>&lt;td&gt;</code> carries a <code>data-label</code>
    attribute (its column name), which the library's ≤720px card-mode CSS uses to
    print a label next to the value automatically.
</p>
